Error [E0121]: `pair` was consumed by a lambda that captures it, so it can't be used here
  --> moved_places_can_be_reinitialized_without_clearing_relatives_4.jet:7:5
    |
  7 |     pair.left = "again"
    |     ^^^^
  --> moved_places_can_be_reinitialized_without_clearing_relatives_4.jet:6:24
    |
  6 |     call(() -> { print(pair) })
    |                        ^^^^ `pair` moved to a lambda that captures it here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `pair` after the move, or give a lambda that captures it a copy with `~pair` where it moved.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
